<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Frontier models · Claude Fable 5.2: when the most powerful Claude is worth it, and how to use it today</title></head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#EEF1F6;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#EEF1F6"><tr><td align="center" style="padding:20px 10px;">
<table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" style="width:600px;max-width:600px;background:#FFFFFF;font-family:'Segoe UI',Arial,sans-serif;color:#101828;border:1px solid #DCE2EC;">
<tr><td style="padding:18px 28px 0;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr>
<td style="font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#5B6578;font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;">INSIGHTS OF THE DAY &nbsp;·&nbsp; Tue 17 Nov 2026</td>
<td align="right" style="font-size:12px;color:#5B6578;">3 min read</td>
</tr></table></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:12px 28px 0;">
<span style="display:inline-block;font-size:12px;font-weight:bold;color:#5B2FC2;background:#EFE9FC;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:10px;">Frontier models</span>
&nbsp;<span style="display:inline-block;font-size:12px;color:#344F8C;background:#E6ECF8;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:10px;">Official + reported</span>
</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:12px 28px 0;font-size:24px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:bold;color:#101828;">Claude Fable 5.2: when the most powerful Claude is worth it, and how to use it today</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:10px 28px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#27324A;">Anthropic released Fable 5.2 on 9 Nov. It is the strongest Claude anyone can use (Mythos 5.2 is the same model, kept for vetted security and life-science teams). Compared with Fable 5.1 it is 20% cheaper, up to 30% faster, and blocks far fewer normal requests. It reads up to 1M tokens and can write up to 128K in one answer.</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:14px 28px 0;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td valign="top" style="padding:0 8px 8px 0;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td bgcolor="#F3F5F9" style="padding:8px 12px;background:#F3F5F9;"><div style="font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;color:#101828;line-height:1.2;">69.9%</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:#5B6578;line-height:1.35;">FrontierSWE v2 coding (Opus 5.5: 62.3%)</div></td></tr></table></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0 8px 8px 0;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td bgcolor="#F3F5F9" style="padding:8px 12px;background:#F3F5F9;"><div style="font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;color:#101828;line-height:1.2;">73.4%</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:#5B6578;line-height:1.35;">reading charts, no tools (Opus 5.5: 64.4%)</div></td></tr></table></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0 8px 8px 0;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td bgcolor="#F3F5F9" style="padding:8px 12px;background:#F3F5F9;"><div style="font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;color:#101828;line-height:1.2;">41.3%</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:#5B6578;line-height:1.35;">Remote Labor Index, about 2x Opus 5.5</div></td></tr></table></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0 8px 8px 0;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td bgcolor="#F3F5F9" style="padding:8px 12px;background:#F3F5F9;"><div style="font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;color:#101828;line-height:1.2;">$8 / $40</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:#5B6578;line-height:1.35;">per M tokens in / out, 2x Opus 5.5</div></td></tr></table></td></tr></table></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px 28px 0;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr>
<td style="border-left:3px solid #5B2FC2;padding:2px 0 2px 14px;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#27324A;">
<div style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1px;font-weight:bold;color:#5B2FC2;font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;">WHY IT MATTERS TO YOU</div>Bigger is not always better. Fable 5.2 at high effort matched Opus 5.5 at max effort on agentic coding for about half the cost per task ($6.72 vs $12.82), but it costs twice as much per token and writes long answers. The smart pattern: Opus 5.5 for everyday work, Fable 5.2 for the hard jobs where other models stall, like refactoring a whole pipeline, reviewing a model end to end, or making sense of a stack of charts and reports.</td>
</tr></table></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:14px 28px 0;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr>
<td bgcolor="#F0F4FF" style="background:#F0F4FF;padding:12px 16px;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#27324A;">
<div style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1px;font-weight:bold;color:#2E4BE0;font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;">TRY IT IN 5 MINUTES</div>Pick one real task that stalled on your usual model, for example turning a messy notebook into a tested module. Run it on Fable 5.2 at medium effort, then the same prompt on Opus 5.5, and compare the result, the time and the tokens. In Claude Code use <code style="font-family:Consolas,\'Courier New\',monospace;font-size:13px;background:#E9EEF7;color:#1F2A44;padding:1px 5px;">/model fable</code> (version 2.1.321 or later). In the API the model id is <code style="font-family:Consolas,\'Courier New\',monospace;font-size:13px;background:#E9EEF7;color:#1F2A44;padding:1px 5px;">claude-fable-5-2</code>.</td>
</tr></table></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:12px 28px 0;"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td bgcolor="#FBE7E7" style="background:#FBE7E7;padding:12px 16px;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#4A1414;"><div style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1px;font-weight:bold;color:#A42727;font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;">ACT TODAY</div>If you are on a Pro plan or a standard Team seat, Fable is included in your plan only until today 1:29 PM IST (16 Nov 11:59 PM PT), for up to half of your weekly limit. Your one free Fable limit reset also expires then: Claude, Settings, Usage, Limit resets, Reset for free. After that, Fable is billed to usage credits.</td></tr></table></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:12px 28px 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:#27324A;"><div style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1px;font-weight:bold;color:#8A5F00;font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;">WATCH OUT</div><div style="padding-top:3px;">- Prompts and agents tuned on Fable 5.1 may behave differently. Test before you switch a pipeline.</div><div style="padding-top:3px;">- Thinking is now always preserved, so API code that edits message history before resending can get 400 errors.</div><div style="padding-top:3px;">- The benchmark numbers are Anthropic's own and not yet independently checked. Measure on your own work.</div></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:10px 28px 0;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#5B6578;"><b style="color:#101828;">Also new:</b> Fable 5.2 is also on Amazon Bedrock, Google Cloud and Microsoft Azure. Fast mode runs up to 2.5x faster at double the price, good for interactive work but not for batch jobs.</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:14px 28px 0;"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr>
